NAME
    cophist - display cartridge coprocessor register history

SYNOPSIS
    cophist [<reg>] [<count>]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the retained register-snapshot history of the active cartridge
    coprocessor (such as SuperFX GSU, SA-1, or NEC DSP), one row per
    refresh, oldest first. The header also reports how many consecutive
    refreshes the registers have remained unchanged.

    On cartridges without a coprocessor, no coprocessor history is
    available.

OPTIONS
    <reg>
        Show history for a single named register (for example, SFR, PBR,
        or R15) instead of all registers.

    <count>
        Number of recent rows to display (default 16).

EXAMPLES
    cophist
    cophist SFR 64
    cophist R15

EXIT STATUS
    0   History printed.
    1   No target attached, invalid argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    copflow(1), regs(1), cpus(1)
